<!-- Buying guide (unique local copy; facts from this page, manufacturer spec pages, and /guides/) -->
<section class="pt-70 pb-30">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-9 guide-body">
        <h2>Who Garden Spas are for</h2>
        <p>Garden Spas are built for people who thought they didn't have room or wiring for a hot tub: condo and townhome owners, small patios, side yards, and even some indoor spaces. They come in nine compact models from 2 to 6 seats and plug into a standard outlet, so the installation is about as simple as a hot tub gets. Maintenance-free Grandwood cabinets keep upkeep low.</p>
        <p>If you live in an HOA community, check your rules about exterior changes before you buy. Our <a href="/service-areas/">service-area pages</a> cover local HOA notes for cities like South Jordan and West Jordan.</p>
        <h2>Plug-and-play: what to expect</h2>
        <p>Garden Spas plug into a standard <strong>120V/15A outlet</strong> using the included 15-foot GFCI cord, so there's no new 240V circuit (HomeGuide's national data puts that at $800–$1,600). The trade-off is heating: on 120V, Garden Spas use a 1.0 kW heater, which raises the water temperature slowly, roughly 1–1.5°F per hour in a 300-gallon spa before heat loss. Keep the cover on between soaks and the spa will be ready when you are. Some models list a 4.0 kW heater for 240V hookups if you want faster heating later. Read <a href="/guides/110v-vs-240v-hot-tubs/">110V vs 240V hot tubs</a> for the full picture.</p>
        <h2>Garden Spas in a Utah winter</h2>
        <p>Garden Spas come with ArcticPac insulation and an ABS bottom, and full foam is available as an option. For winter soaking in Utah, we recommend the full-foam option, a tight-fitting cover, and shorter soaks with the lid closed between sessions. See our <a href="/guides/hot-tub-utah-winter/">winter guide</a>.</p>
        <h2>See Garden Spas in Midvale</h2>
        <p>We keep display models from every brand we carry at 6905 S State St in Midvale (Mon–Sat, 10 AM–5 PM). Floor models change, so <a href="/contact/">call or message us</a> if you want to sit in a specific model before you visit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

